      "step_id": "tile_python_comprehensions_iterating.s01",
      "type": "explainer",
      "concept_ids": [
        "python.comprehensions"
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Comprehensions",
      "title": "Building lists and dicts in one line: comprehensions",
      "lede": "Replace multi-line loops with compact, readable expressions.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "block_id": "tile_python_comprehensions_iterating.s01.h1",
          "text": "Building lists and dicts in one line: comprehensions",
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_python_comprehensions_iterating.s01.p1",
          "text": "Building a new list from an existing one by looping is common enough that Python has a shorthand for it. A list comprehension consists of brackets containing an expression followed by a for clause, and optionally one or more for or if clauses; it produces a new list by evaluating the expression for each item — [minutes * 2 for minutes in delivery_times] doubles every value.",
          "role": "definition",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "python.comprehensions"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "python.comprehensions#f1"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "python.comprehensions#tb1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "block_id": "tile_python_comprehensions_iterating.s01.p2",
          "text": "Add an if clause to filter the source: [minutes for minutes in delivery_times if minutes >= 45] keeps only the delivery times that satisfy that condition. Dict comprehensions work the same way with curly braces and a key: value expression — {city: len(city) for city in ('Lagos', 'Abuja', 'Kano')} maps each city name to its length.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "python.comprehensions"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "python.comprehensions#f2",
              "python.comprehensions#f3"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "python.comprehensions#tb2",
              "python.comprehensions#tb3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "before_after",
          "block_id": "tile_python_comprehensions_iterating.s01.ba1",
          "before": {
            "type": "code_walkthrough",
            "block_id": "tile_python_comprehensions_iterating.s01.ba1.before",
            "language": "python",
            "code": "# Multi-line loop\ndoubled = []\nfor minutes in delivery_times:\n    if minutes >= 45:\n        doubled.append(minutes * 2)",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "start_line": 2,
                "end_line": 2,
                "text": "empty list to collect results"
              },
              {
                "start_line": 3,
                "end_line": 3,
                "text": "for clause: iterate over source"
              },
              {
                "start_line": 4,
                "end_line": 4,
                "text": "if clause: filter condition"
              },
              {
                "start_line": 5,
                "end_line": 5,
                "text": "expression: double each kept value"
              }
            ],
            "reveal": "all"
          },
          "after": {
            "type": "code_walkthrough",
            "block_id": "tile_python_comprehensions_iterating.s01.ba1.after",
            "language": "python",
            "code": "# Equivalent list comprehension\ndoubled = [minutes * 2 for minutes in delivery_times if minutes >= 45]",
            "annotations": [
              {
                "start_line": 2,
                "end_line": 2,
                "text": "expression · for clause · if clause — all in one line"
              }
            ],
            "reveal": "all"
          },
          "change_summary": "Five lines collapse to one: the expression, for clause and if clause move inside brackets.",
          "lineage": {
