        "public": {
          "prompt": "A colleague writes this code and expects the cities to print in the order `Lagos`, `Abuja`, `Kano`:\n\n```python\ncities = {'Lagos', 'Abuja', 'Kano'}\nfor city in cities:\n    print(city)\n```\n\nWhat is wrong with that expectation?",
          "options": [
            {
              "option_id": "opt_a",
              "text": "A set is unordered, so the items may come out in any order"
            },
            {
              "option_id": "opt_b",
              "text": "Nothing — sets always iterate in insertion order"
            },
